      notes: `A selection: Part I chs. I–III were asked for; the rest of the book was searched for quotations of the Timaeus and Critias, and the two chapters that retell or quote the dialogues' story as their subject were added. ${DONNELLY_NOT_IMPORTED} ${DONNELLY_REJECTED} ${DONNELLY_RACIAL} The book was much reprinted from its plates as numbered 'editions' and was the main modern source for later Atlantis writers: W. Scott-Elliot's The Story of Atlantis (1896) names it.`,
